WEBVTT

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:23.790
Your initials I wrote in my notebook

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:31.600
Discreetly overlapping so they won't be noticed

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:37.110
I stretched up

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:42.110
The school building I looked up at and the distant sky

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:53.690
The moon in broad daylight shows some restraint and lingers inside the light.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:01:01.310
I want these feelings to reach you

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:59.520
my heart

00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:11.500
I embrace the small bud of passion that sprouted in my heart

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:13.880
I close my eyes

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:18.170
Some day I want to make it bloom into a big flower

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:15.750
someday

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:26.940
Our fluttering hearts connected, our eyes exchanging a glance

00:01:40.010 --> 00:01:40.580
I...

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:47.580
I like you, Yoshizuki.

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:53.460
I said it! I finally said it!

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:15.530
Me too.

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:20.820
I like you too, Seto-kun...

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:37.570
...as well as Teratani-kun, Yuka, Nami and everyone else in our class.

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:38.840
I like them all.

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:44.250
It's such a shame we'll all be split up soon.

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:46.110
It's kind of sad.

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:47.770
Uh... no...

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:51.510
Yoshizuki, that's not really what I'm saying.

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:55.570
Iori, look! We got so many toys out of the crane game!

00:02:55.570 --> 00:02:57.720
Wow! That's awesome!

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:00.330
Right? It turns out Teratani's really good at them!

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:02.810
Oh, really? Oh! This is so cute!

00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:04.330
Isn't it?!

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:07.160
What?! You told her?

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:07.950
I did.

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:11.090
And what was her answer?!

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:15.460
Iori-chan was too drunk to understand what I meant.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.770
She said "I like you too, Seto-kun..."

00:03:17.770 --> 00:03:22.290
"...as well as Teratani-kun, and everyone else in our class. I like them all."

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:24.370
Oh, man...

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:27.420
She might have deliberately evaded giving me a straight answer.

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:29.610
What do you mean evaded?

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:33.480
She might have sidestepped it to avoid hurting me.

00:03:33.850 --> 00:03:36.860
Why do you always assume the worst case?

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:40.360
Because... it took all my courage just to say it...

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:43.040
What if it was the opposite?

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:47.540
What if she was embarrassed and just pretended to be drunk?

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:49.750
But it didn't seem like that.

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:52.010
Did you forget?

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:52.620
About what?

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:55.130
She's in the Drama Club.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:58.930
Find out at the next place we go.

00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:00.650
I'll draw Morisaki away...

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:02.860
...and give you guys some alone time.

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:06.270
That's what we were planning anyway...

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:08.670
Huh? Did you say something?

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:11.730
Oh, no! Not really!

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:15.010
Anyway, you've said it once already!

00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:18.450
You better settle it tonight!

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:20.940
Tonight is Christmas Eve!

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:23.110
A miracle's sure to happen!

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:25.240
Certainly...

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:30.120
...I think tonight will be my last chance.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:33.160
Karaoke

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:33.160
Yashiki

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:36.250
Sorry! Thanks for waiting!

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:38.290
Hey, where are we going next?

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:44.670
Well, it's no fun if we all go to the same place.

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:47.140
Let's split up into boy and girl pairs and go somewhere separately!

00:04:48.630 --> 00:04:53.350
Well actually, Ichitaka said he wants to be alone with Yoshizuki.

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:57.110
What? Really? Seto-kun, that's so brave!

00:04:57.110 --> 00:04:58.610
Uh, well...

00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:02.370
Seriously, huh? It's such a pain!

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:02.370
It's so embarrassing!

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:03.900
Teratani...

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:06.670
You better take Morisaki on a proper date too!

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:09.990
Yuka...

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:13.170
Why don't you take the opportunity to have a good time?

00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:14.120
Iori...

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.610
Then, let's get going, Morisaki.

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:17.500
Sure...

00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:24.530
Good luck, Yuka.

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:27.870
Thank you, Seto-kun.

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:30.350
I know you're doing all this for Yuka.

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:34.000
What about us?

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:36.950
What do you want to do now?

00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:40.190
I'm sure you've still got plenty of study to do. Why don't we just head home?

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:41.400
Oh, wait a second!

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:45.410
Since we had a lot to drink,

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:48.080
I want to sober up before I go back and start studying.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.830
How about a stroll?

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:53.540
That's fine with me.

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:35.190
First...

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:38.240
First, I need to find an opportunity to confess!

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:40.890
What am I supposed to talk about? What should I say?

00:06:50.070 --> 00:06:51.720
Feeling a little more sober?

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:54.970
Oh, yes, thanks.

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:58.390
Seto-kun, are you going to study during the winter break?

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:00.900
Well, I think so.

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:03.450
Which college are you trying to get into?

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:05.900
Didn't I tell you?

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:06.400
No.

00:07:06.830 --> 00:07:08.690
There we go! This is the perfect topic!

00:07:09.310 --> 00:07:11.600
It's the same place you're trying to get in.

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:12.450
Takashiki University.

00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:14.370
Is something wrong?

00:07:15.110 --> 00:07:15.870
No...

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:17.240
What is it?

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:22.070
I actually decided not to go to college.

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:26.410
Then, after you graduate?

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:30.720
Seto-kun, do you know the name, Kaminogi Isai?

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:34.010
I'm pretty sure I recognise it.

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:37.450
He's a famous theatre director.

00:07:37.450 --> 00:07:40.100
I very much respect him.

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:43.380
It's been my dream to join his theatre group.

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:47.450
So, I auditioned to join his theatre last month.

00:07:47.450 --> 00:07:49.870
I didn't expect to pass the audition,

00:07:49.870 --> 00:07:51.900
but by a stroke of luck, they accepted me.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:54.530
What?! Are you serious?! That's great!

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:56.700
It was just luck, that's all.

00:07:57.070 --> 00:08:00.190
No, it's because you have talent.

00:08:00.190 --> 00:08:02.250
But, that's amazing.

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:05.360
Taking hold of your dream with your own two hands.

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:09.800
It took a long time to convince my parents.

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:13.730
But Isai-san and another staff member from the production company...

00:08:13.730 --> 00:08:16.150
...worked hard to help me convince them.

00:08:16.150 --> 00:08:18.850
That means they have really high hopes for you, doesn't it?

00:08:18.850 --> 00:08:21.350
It's not as big a deal as you think.

00:08:22.010 --> 00:08:26.360
You must be happy, knowing what you want to do in life.

00:08:27.090 --> 00:08:28.450
What about you, Seto-kun?

00:08:28.450 --> 00:08:30.320
Why did you decide to go for Takashiki University?

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:33.200
What? Well, that is to say...

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:40.080
Actually, I-

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:41.920
What?

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:44.580
Hey, look! That movie...

00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:49.350
That movie's being shown in theatres now...

00:08:49.350 --> 00:08:52.860
Is Itsuki-chan on the staff, by any chance?

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:54.870
What? How did you know that?

00:08:54.870 --> 00:08:56.630
Am I right?

00:08:56.630 --> 00:09:00.900
A magazine article I read mentioned a Japanese teen girl...

00:09:00.900 --> 00:09:03.270
...who worked on the movie as an SF sculpture artist.

00:09:03.720 --> 00:09:07.380
I see. So it really was Itsuki-chan.

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:08.920
That's amazing!

00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:11.160
Hey, have you seen the movie yet?

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:13.370
No, I've been studying for the entrance exam.

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:15.340
That's no good! You should see the movie.

00:09:15.340 --> 00:09:16.300
Hey, Yoshizuki-

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:19.280
Hey, why don't we go and see it right now?

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:21.240
It's already closed.

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:22.950
That's not what I meant.

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:26.130
Take a picture in front of a theatre, and e-mail it to her.

00:09:26.130 --> 00:09:27.550
I'll help you.

00:09:27.550 --> 00:09:28.870
No, don't worry about it.

00:09:28.870 --> 00:09:32.050
Why not? Itsuki-chan will be happy if you do.

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:33.340
I said you don't need to!

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:41.480
I'm sorry. Did I say something wrong?

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:43.970
No, it's not that.

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:51.480
"This is an order! Hurry up and make Iori-san yours."

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:55.690
I made a promise to Itsuki.

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:57.360
A promise?

00:09:58.670 --> 00:10:01.870
Yoshizuki, I...

00:10:05.510 --> 00:10:07.100
Just a second.

00:10:08.350 --> 00:10:09.510
Hello.

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:11.540
Oh, good evening.

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:14.270
Now?

00:10:14.270 --> 00:10:15.960
I'm in Shibuya.

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:20.180
What? Right now?

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:23.890
Isai-san recommended me?

00:10:24.610 --> 00:10:27.460
I understand. I'll be there as soon as possible.

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:30.350
What's up?

00:10:30.840 --> 00:10:33.610
That was the production agency.

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:35.860
They want me to come to an audition for a TV commercial right away.

00:10:36.420 --> 00:10:38.660
What? Right now?

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:41.050
The person who was supposed to attend the audition cancelled.

00:10:41.050 --> 00:10:44.340
And Isai-san said I should try out in their place.

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:49.560
Are you all right? Do you want me to come with you?

00:10:49.560 --> 00:10:52.620
I couldn't ask you to do that.

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:54.880
Don't worry about me. Okay?

00:11:17.830 --> 00:11:20.150
How long does the audition take?

00:11:20.810 --> 00:11:22.360
I don't know.

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:25.830
Sorry, I'm sure you're very nervous right now.

00:11:34.830 --> 00:11:36.710
Is this how it's going to end?

00:11:43.270 --> 00:11:46.380
Thanks for coming all the way here with me.

00:11:47.080 --> 00:11:48.350
Well, I better go now.

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:49.310
Yoshizuki...

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:54.810
I'll wait for you at the coffee shop until you finish the audition.

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:56.910
I can't let you do something like that.

00:11:56.910 --> 00:11:58.650
Besides, I don't even know when I'll be finished.

00:11:59.040 --> 00:12:01.030
It doesn't matter how long it takes.

00:12:01.540 --> 00:12:02.840
Seto-kun?

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:04.530
Anyway, I'll be waiting.

00:12:08.850 --> 00:12:10.040
Iori-chan.

00:12:10.610 --> 00:12:13.330
Everybody's waiting for you. Hurry up.

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:14.080
Oh, yes.

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:16.630
Have you been drinking?

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:19.760
I'm sorry. Just a little.

00:12:21.740 --> 00:12:23.340
I suppose it can't be helped.

00:12:23.670 --> 00:12:28.360
Well, just do your best. This will be a good experience for you.

00:12:28.360 --> 00:12:29.810
Yes.

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:38.190
Are you her boyfriend or something?

00:12:39.330 --> 00:12:41.750
Uh... no. Not really.

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:46.280
That girl is a golden egg to us, you see.

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:48.990
Don't lay your hands on her.

00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:52.740
Thank you for accompanying her here.

00:12:52.740 --> 00:12:54.620
For today, take this and go home.

00:12:55.910 --> 00:12:56.880
No, thank you.

00:12:57.400 --> 00:13:01.070
And besides, I promised to wait for her.

00:13:01.070 --> 00:13:04.840
I don't know what time the audition will end.

00:13:05.990 --> 00:13:07.140
I don't mind.

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:11.300
We will take her home.

00:13:11.300 --> 00:13:13.770
Our agency has the responsibility for that.

00:13:14.460 --> 00:13:16.860
I'll tell her you had already gone home.

00:13:16.860 --> 00:13:17.880
But!

00:13:17.880 --> 00:13:21.400
You're just wasting your time. Hurry on home.

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:24.760
I guess she's not coming.

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:27.530
Looking back on the past two years...

00:14:27.530 --> 00:14:29.760
I had so many chances to let her know how I felt.

00:14:33.610 --> 00:14:35.760
But I didn't have the courage...

00:14:35.760 --> 00:14:36.960
...and couldn't do it...

00:14:37.960 --> 00:14:39.830
Rather than the miracle of Christmas Eve,

00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:42.340
It's more like my punishment, I guess.

00:14:44.350 --> 00:14:45.820
Tonight is Christmas Eve!

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:47.360
A miracle's sure to happen!

00:14:48.420 --> 00:14:52.370
It must be the end for me if I'm relying on your words like this.

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:01.120
Seto-kun!

00:15:03.690 --> 00:15:06.090
Yoshizuki? Why are you here?

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:10.670
I couldn't help but think, "What if Seto-kun was still waiting for me?"

00:15:10.670 --> 00:15:11.890
What about the people from your agency?

00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:13.410
Don't worry.

00:15:13.410 --> 00:15:15.640
I made some up and slipped out.

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:22.540
Oh yeah, this.

00:15:22.540 --> 00:15:23.700
What?

00:15:23.700 --> 00:15:25.980
Could you give this back to that manager person?

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:26.780
Okay.

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:30.110
Hey, Seto-kun, do you still have some time?

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:32.360
Yes.

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:34.120
Come with me.

00:15:34.690 --> 00:15:36.620
There's something I want you to see.

00:15:44.680 --> 00:15:46.720
There she is.

00:15:46.720 --> 00:15:50.230
I'd better tell her to cut ties with that boy.

00:15:50.230 --> 00:15:53.920
Don't worry. It's just a matter of time.

00:15:53.920 --> 00:15:57.760
Soon, the entire country will know who she is.

00:15:57.760 --> 00:16:03.310
Then, she'll realise her own potential.

00:16:09.450 --> 00:16:11.610
Yoshizuki, where are you taking me?

00:16:11.900 --> 00:16:14.070
Just come with me quickly.

00:16:38.550 --> 00:16:40.210
It's beautiful!

00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:47.290
I wonder what it feels like...

00:16:47.810 --> 00:16:48.520
What?

00:16:49.890 --> 00:16:52.540
To spend Christmas with the one you love...

00:16:52.540 --> 00:16:54.570
I wonder what that's like.

00:17:08.130 --> 00:17:11.620
Hey, does Teratani-kun have someone he likes?

00:17:11.620 --> 00:17:12.860
Who knows?

00:17:12.860 --> 00:17:14.980
I don't think there's anyone at the moment, but...

00:17:14.980 --> 00:17:17.530
...we really haven't talked about that kind of stuff lately.

00:17:17.530 --> 00:17:20.040
He's got such a poker face...

00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:22.960
He'd probably act normally, even in front of the person he likes.

00:17:22.960 --> 00:17:24.100
Maybe.

00:17:25.110 --> 00:17:28.150
I wish he was easy to read, like you are.

00:17:29.290 --> 00:17:31.370
What do you mean I'm easy to read?

00:17:31.940 --> 00:17:33.800
It's easy to see, when I look at you.

00:17:33.800 --> 00:17:35.110
I can tell who you like.

00:17:36.630 --> 00:17:39.140
Yuka's the only one who thinks otherwise.

00:17:39.140 --> 00:17:41.030
She thinks you like me.

00:17:41.030 --> 00:17:42.200
Funny, isn't it?

00:17:43.880 --> 00:17:47.290
Don't worry. I know who you really like.

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:51.590
The one you really like is Itsuki-chan.

00:17:55.280 --> 00:17:56.790
I know that.

00:18:00.060 --> 00:18:02.680
Oh, I'm sorry. It's none of my business.

00:18:11.100 --> 00:18:13.920
Yoshizuki, are you still drunk?

00:18:13.920 --> 00:18:17.200
Huh? Was I that drunk before?

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:20.090
What? Don't you remember?

00:18:20.090 --> 00:18:22.410
You were ranting on and...

00:18:22.410 --> 00:18:24.460
Oh, no! Really?

00:18:24.460 --> 00:18:26.270
I'm not sure exactly.

00:18:26.270 --> 00:18:30.770
But you were so persistent. Going on like "Do you want to hear who I like?"

00:18:30.770 --> 00:18:36.230
"He's so totally cool, sweet, and very funny," and so on.

00:18:46.490 --> 00:18:47.350
Liar.

00:18:50.330 --> 00:18:53.820
No matter how drunk I was, I'd never brag like that.

00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:54.690
Why?

00:18:57.000 --> 00:18:58.570
I'm sure he doesn't like me back.

00:19:00.550 --> 00:19:04.330
I see. There is somebody you like.

00:19:04.330 --> 00:19:05.070
Yes.

00:19:06.280 --> 00:19:09.000
It's a KO before I'm even in the ring, huh?

00:19:09.980 --> 00:19:10.940
Nothing.

00:19:24.430 --> 00:19:27.060
It's that late already?

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:28.680
Let's get going!

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:29.550
Yes.

00:19:29.550 --> 00:19:32.420
Sorry for dragging you all over the place.

00:19:32.420 --> 00:19:35.290
That's all right. I'll walk with you to the station.

00:19:35.290 --> 00:19:37.970
It's fine! You don't have to go <i>that</i> far.

00:19:37.970 --> 00:19:39.820
We're taking the same train anyway.

00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:41.280
Oh, that's right.

00:19:46.420 --> 00:19:47.600
Yoshizuki!

00:19:48.920 --> 00:19:49.660
Listen to me.

00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:50.660
Actually...

00:19:51.090 --> 00:19:51.870
Actually, I-

00:19:56.810 --> 00:19:58.470
It's Yuka.

00:19:58.470 --> 00:19:59.860
Hi, how did it go?

00:19:59.860 --> 00:20:01.470
Uh...

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:03.640
Hello, Yuka? What's wrong?

00:20:14.390 --> 00:20:15.470
Yuka?

00:20:20.710 --> 00:20:21.660
Iori...

00:20:21.660 --> 00:20:23.090
What's wrong?

00:20:30.210 --> 00:20:33.910
Seto-kun, when you see Teratani,

00:20:33.910 --> 00:20:34.920
tell him to drop dead!

00:20:36.090 --> 00:20:37.540
Did he reject you?

00:20:38.240 --> 00:20:39.030
Why?!

00:20:39.030 --> 00:20:40.660
I don't know!

00:20:40.660 --> 00:20:42.760
He just told me that he can't have a relationship with me.

00:20:43.370 --> 00:20:48.010
But, I don't think he has someone who he likes.

00:20:48.010 --> 00:20:49.750
Seto-kun...

00:20:49.750 --> 00:20:52.720
I'm sorry, but let's call it a day.

00:20:52.720 --> 00:20:54.900
I'll take Yuka home.

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:58.790
It's fine Iori. I'd feel bad to Seto-kun, then.

00:20:58.790 --> 00:20:59.780
But...

00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:04.050
I didn't mean to call you for this.

00:21:04.050 --> 00:21:06.720
I'm all right. I can go back by myself.

00:21:06.720 --> 00:21:09.080
Don't say something sad like that!

00:21:10.770 --> 00:21:13.420
You shouldn't say things like that.

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:17.340
We're friends, aren't we?

00:21:22.640 --> 00:21:24.300
I'll find out what's going on.

00:21:26.350 --> 00:21:27.800
I'll find out why he rejected Morisaki.

00:21:31.090 --> 00:21:33.560
You want to know why as well, don't you?

00:21:33.950 --> 00:21:35.560
Seto-kun...

00:21:47.610 --> 00:21:50.430
The number you are trying to reach is currently out of service range,

00:21:50.430 --> 00:21:53.430
or is switched off and cannot be reached.

00:21:58.610 --> 00:22:00.080
Yuka...

00:22:14.400 --> 00:22:15.840
Teratani!

00:22:15.840 --> 00:22:17.100
Huh, Ichitaka?

00:22:21.860 --> 00:22:24.630
Man, that hurts...

00:22:24.630 --> 00:22:27.670
I never thought you'd hit me.

00:22:27.670 --> 00:22:30.540
Why did you reject Morisaki?

00:22:31.930 --> 00:22:34.870
Why couldn't you accept her feelings?

00:22:35.600 --> 00:22:38.040
She was serious about you!

00:22:38.620 --> 00:22:41.080
It's because she was serious that I couldn't accept her.

00:22:47.170 --> 00:22:48.800
Now we're even.

00:22:49.890 --> 00:22:51.260
Teratani?

00:22:52.400 --> 00:22:55.540
Morisaki's serious about her feelings for me...

00:22:55.540 --> 00:22:58.550
...but I only see her as a friend.

00:22:59.230 --> 00:23:01.050
If I just went for it,

00:23:01.050 --> 00:23:03.480
it might end up hurting her more.

00:23:04.480 --> 00:23:09.290
Anyhow, if you have time to stick your nose into someone else's relationship,

00:23:09.290 --> 00:23:11.520
why don't you take care of your own?

00:23:11.520 --> 00:23:13.850
No... it's no good.

00:23:15.700 --> 00:23:17.250
I just don't think it's possible...

00:23:19.040 --> 00:23:20.800
So many things got in the way.

00:23:20.800 --> 00:23:22.460
Fate's giving me a sign.

00:23:33.260 --> 00:23:50.280
Higashi Matsubara

00:23:33.280 --> 00:23:37.800
Train approaching. Please stay behind the white line.

00:23:54.710 --> 00:23:58.840
Thank you for everything today, both of you.

00:23:58.840 --> 00:24:00.000
It's all right.

00:24:01.710 --> 00:24:03.010
Good night.

00:24:13.770 --> 00:24:19.650
That Teratani... He could have at least shown her a good time for tonight.

00:24:19.650 --> 00:24:22.890
I'm sure that was Teratani-kun's way of trying to be as sincere as possible.

00:24:22.890 --> 00:24:24.710
I know that, but...

00:24:27.460 --> 00:24:28.900
Things didn't go as we hoped for, huh?

00:24:29.670 --> 00:24:31.810
I thought we'd planned it out well.

00:24:32.790 --> 00:24:35.560
But if a relationship could be handled that easily,

00:24:35.560 --> 00:24:37.430
no one would suffer from love.

00:24:37.430 --> 00:24:39.250
Reality's tough.

00:24:39.960 --> 00:24:42.970
In the end, I didn't get to confess either.

00:24:44.450 --> 00:24:46.850
Who were you planning to confess to?

00:24:47.790 --> 00:24:48.780
To you.

00:25:15.520 --> 00:25:18.830
Next stop is Meidaimae. Meidaimae.

00:25:31.510 --> 00:25:32.850
No way...

00:25:34.000 --> 00:25:35.980
Not even a single word?

00:25:51.840 --> 00:25:54.860
I thought it was just a one-sided crush...

00:26:20.730 --> 00:26:28.380
The worn-out diary

00:26:28.380 --> 00:26:36.020
I left behind in a corner of the classroom

00:26:36.020 --> 00:26:44.460
I closed it softly. I hold this throbbing in my heart

00:26:44.460 --> 00:26:55.260
In both hands and warm it up

00:26:55.260 --> 00:27:02.500
Since that day I met you by chance,

00:27:02.500 --> 00:27:10.160
I've grown small wings

00:27:10.160 --> 00:27:17.550
I felt your kind gaze,

00:27:17.550 --> 00:27:25.520
And even now I have a feeling I could fly into the sky

00:27:25.520 --> 00:27:29.110
Staring eyes and eyes
